From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:15:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 019/147] quality monitor: show the transport on every platform

The quality monitor named the transport only for WebRTC sessions on the web.
It now shows it on every platform next to Delay, FPS and Codec: 'WebRTC' for a
direct session, 'WebSocket (relay)' or 'Relay' for one relayed through hbbr
(the punch path names its relay 'Relay', which the connection dialog shows as
TCP), so a laggy session can be told apart from a relayed one while testing.

(Research patch transport-latency 8.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/models/model.dart | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/models/model.dart b/flutter/lib/models/model.dart
index f1abb8e..964f213 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/models/model.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/models/model.dart
@@ -3902,15 +3902,19 @@ class QualityMonitorModel with ChangeNotifier {
   bool get show => _show;
   QualityMonitorData get data => _data;
 
-  // Only a WebRTC session on the web names its transport here: web has no
-  // session tab to show it on (the desktop tab's tooltip already does), and
-  // WebRTC is the one path that can be direct or TURN.
+  // The transport the session runs on, next to its delay and frame rate, so a
+  // laggy session can be told apart from a relayed one. WebRTC is the one path
+  // that can be direct or TURN.
   String? get webrtcTransport {
-    if (!isWeb) return null;
     final ffiModel = parent.target?.ffiModel;
     if (ffiModel == null) return null;
     final streamType = ffiModel.cachedPeerData.streamType;
-    if (!streamType.startsWith('WebRTC')) return null;
+    if (streamType.isEmpty) return null;
+    if (!streamType.startsWith('WebRTC')) {
+      // 'Relay' names itself; the connection dialog shows it as TCP.
+      if (streamType == 'Relay') return streamType;
+      return ffiModel.direct == false ? '$streamType (relay)' : streamType;
+    }
     return ffiModel.direct == false ? '$streamType (TURN)' : streamType;
   }
 
